Subject: Merging rkward-users and rkward-devel mailing lists
Message-ID: <20250927105334.4489e8ae@booklife>

Hi,

as subscribers, most of you will be aware that RKWard has two main
mailing lists: rkward-devel at kde.org, and rkward-users at kde.org.
Historically, the motivation for creating rkward-users (a few years
after rkward-devel) was not to actually keep discussions separate, but
to encourage participation from users, who might otherwise be reluctant
to post to a "-devel" mailing list, perhaps after witnessing the
sometimes harsh rebuffs for doing so some other lists.

Nonetheless, communication has rather been moving away from e-mail, and
of the modest traffic on both lists, much has been double-posts, and/or
"inappropriate content" in the sense that usage-questions evolved into
implementation discussions or vice-versa.

Long story short, I intend to request a merge of these two lists into a
single list rkward at kde.org. Your subscription should remain active,
automatically, but if subscribed with different addresses, you may be
subscribed twice after the merge, and you may need to adjust filters in
your mail client.

If there are any objections to this step, please speak up, within a
week.

For completeness, I'll point out that there is also the list
rkward-tracker at kde.org, which receives automated messages about commit
messages, failures in automated builds, etc., which can be quite "noisy"
at times. I do not currently intend to change anything about this list,
even though a lot of that info can also be received by subscribing to
individual notifications via invent.kde.org.

Regards
Thomas
